# RTL Engineering Rules (Cursor)

For UI rendering Persian (fa), Arabic (ar) or Hebrew (he). Copy this file to
`.cursor/rules/rtl.mdc`. Copilot users: `copilot-instructions.md`; Codex CLI users:
`AGENTS.md` — same rules, native formats.

## Hard rules

- RTL pages: `<html lang="fa" dir="rtl">` (or ar/he). Never `dir="ltr"` on RTL-only content.
- LTR host pages (es/en): root stays LTR; each RTL region gets `dir="rtl"`; embedded RTL runs
  in prose get `<bdi>`.
- Logical CSS only: `margin-inline-start/end`, `padding-inline-start/end`,
  `inset-inline-start/end`, `text-align: start/end`. Never `margin-left/right`,
  `padding-left/right`, `text-align: left/right`, physical `left:/right:` in RTL contexts.
- No `letter-spacing` on Arabic-script text — it breaks cursive joining (م د ی ر ی ت).
  Hebrew: discouraged (nikud clipping), not forbidden.
- Persian ZWNJ (U+200C): `می‌شود`, `خانه‌ها`, `بیشتر‌ین` — half-space, never a full space.
  No ZWNJ in Arabic or Hebrew.
- Isolate mixed-direction runs: URLs, emails, `$99`, phones inside RTL prose → `<bdi>` or
  `dir="auto"`. Otherwise `$99` scrambles to `99$`.
- Numerals by profile: fa ۰-۹ · ar ٠-٩ · he 0-9 · es 0-9. Never convert digits in code, URLs
  or APIs.
- Line-height ≥ 1.5 body (1.6 recommended) for Arabic script; Hebrew needs nikud headroom.
- Fonts: fa — Vazirmatn / Sahel / IRANSansX · ar — Noto Naskh Arabic / Cairo / Tajawal ·
  he — Heebo / Assistant / Rubik. A Latin-only stack is a defect.

## Tailwind

- `ms-/me-/ps-/pe-/text-start/text-end` instead of `ml-/mr-/pl-/pr-/text-left/text-right`.
- Directional motion: `translate-x-4 rtl:-translate-x-4`.
- Flip direction-aware icons (`rtl:-scale-x-100`): arrows, chevrons, indent, reply, exit,
  forward. Never flip: logos, media controls, clocks, avatars, checkmarks.

## Dates

- fa: `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('fa-IR')` → Jalali + Persian digits.
- he: `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('he-IL-u-ca-hebrew')` → Hebrew calendar.
- Store ISO-8601 UTC; format at render; format server-side for SSR to avoid hydration drift.

## Spanish (LTR host) specifics

- RAE inverted marks ¿ ¡ mandatory on questions/exclamations.
- «comillas angulares» in prose; embedded Arabic/Hebrew runs must be isolated (`<bdi>`).

## Verify before shipping

```bash
pip install raast
raast doctor . --language fa   # or ar / he / es
```

